{"ts":"2026-08-02T21:05:22.040Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"5e676b30ed4e8585ecf5ff9e","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-inn5y5"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Acceptance criteria are documented as merging like tags but are stored as one delimiter-joined scalar, so concurrent criteria additions from different branches are silently discarded"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"src/core/item/parse.ts:92 documents applyAcceptanceCriteriaMutations as giving --add-ac/--remove-ac 'tag-API parity' with the explicit promise that 'disjoint additions merge cleanly across branches'. Tags have that property because 'tags' is in ITEM_UNION_COLLECTION_FIELDS and merges by element identity. acceptance_criteria is not in that list: it is stored as a single string joined with '; ', so it takes the scalar three-way path and resolves toward the preferred side like any other scalar. The documented guarantee is therefore false for the one field whose CLI grammar is explicitly list-shaped. Criteria are the field close-validation reads, so the loss is silent in exactly the workflow that is supposed to be enforced."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["acceptance-criteria","concurrency","data-loss","merge"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-02T21:05:22.040Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-02T21:05:22.040Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":240},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Concurrent disjoint --add-ac additions on separate branches all survive a merge, or the delimiter-joined scalar semantics are documented at src/core/item/parse.ts, in pm update --help, and in the merge guidance; Every field whose CLI grammar exposes additive and subtractive mutation is either a union collection or is listed as a known-lossy scalar in one enumerable place the merge driver and the docs both read; A merge that discards acceptance criteria names acceptance_criteria and the number of discarded criteria in the receipt guidance rather than reporting a generic scalar conflict"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/value","value":"Acceptance criteria are the machine-readable definition of done; losing them on merge silently weakens every close-time check built on them."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/impact","value":"Any two agents that add criteria to the same item on different branches lose all but one contribution, and the close validation that reads criteria cannot tell."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/outcome","value":"Either acceptance criteria merge by element identity like every other list-shaped field, or the docstring and the CLI help state the scalar semantics and pm warns when a merge discards criteria."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/why_now","value":"The same probe that falsified merge-direction independence falsified this documented guarantee; the fix is small and the loss is unrecoverable."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-33cw"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/environment","value":"git merge via pm merge drivers; pm 2026.8.2"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/repro_steps","value":"Create an item on a base commit, branch three ways, run pm update <id> --add-ac 'criterion from A|B|C' on each branch, commit, then merge all three branches into one clone."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"All three disjoint criteria survive, matching the tag-API parity documented at src/core/item/parse.ts:92."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Exactly one criterion survives: acceptance_criteria = 'criterion from A'. The other two appear only as discarded_hash values in the merge receipt. No warning names acceptance_criteria as a lossy field."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"core/item/parse"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"aa4c26c143dded4aa2ab326e17fd27283dd210d50efceff3515e1636a8a5d316","message":""}
